.SH FILES
.TP
${HOME}/.asoundrc
Ardopcf will look for an ALSA source and sink named ARDOP and try to use
those, if you did not specify an audio device at invocation.
Note that DMIX/DSNOOP do not currently work with ardopcf.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The following diagnostics may be issued on stdout:
.TP
Error in InitSound(). Stopping ardop.
Usually this means you did not specify a proper audio device, or it is
busy.
.PP
\f[B]ardopcf\f[R] does not provide error standard error codes that can
be used by scripts, but a log file will be created and written to, the
amount writen depending on your settings.
See the section above \[lq]Other Options.\[rq]
.SH BUGS
Sometimes when connecting to a remote station that runs ARDOP_WIN
implementation, an endless IDLE/ACK loop will be entered.
.PP
DMIX/DSNOOP ALSA plugins do not work with ardopcf due to a workaround
needed for a kernel change around 5.15.
